1
00:01:43,791 --> 00:01:45,042
What are we gonna do with it, huh?

2
00:01:45,126 --> 00:01:47,503
Oh, this Sandy is mine.
Always has been.

3
00:01:47,586 --> 00:01:49,255
Why is this one began to chipped?

4
00:01:49,338 --> 00:01:52,174
Uninstalling it
is gonna cost us, so are you ready?

5
00:01:52,258 --> 00:01:54,051
Ugh. It'll spike us shit.

6
00:01:54,135 --> 00:01:56,387
He's a massive pain in my ass.

7
00:01:56,470 --> 00:01:58,347
How about we flat-line them?

8
00:01:58,430 --> 00:02:01,725
The five Fingers can have discount
on work created on his cold dead body.

9
00:02:01,809 --> 00:02:03,227
We still need a reaper for that.

10
00:02:03,310 --> 00:02:05,062
But we'd breakeven, wouldn't we?

11
00:02:05,146 --> 00:02:06,522
Sure, barely. I suppose.

12
00:02:06,605 --> 00:02:10,401
You hear that? I should just
rip the damn thing off myself.

13
00:02:10,484 --> 00:02:14,321
Maybe then you'd finally learn not to
clap-shit that ain't yours, piss sniffer.

14
00:02:14,905 --> 00:02:16,574
Please don't get blood all over my room,

15
00:02:16,657 --> 00:02:17,700
-all right?
-Stay out of this!

16
00:02:17,783 --> 00:02:20,536
Um, excuse me?
I was the one who found him.

17
00:02:20,619 --> 00:02:21,704
Grr.

18
00:02:23,247 --> 00:02:25,374
-You fucking lied to me?
-Shut up!

19
00:02:25,457 --> 00:02:28,752
Now, spill it. What the fuck you're doing
and parading around on my throne?

20
00:02:28,836 --> 00:02:30,212
Yours?

21
00:02:30,296 --> 00:02:32,381
You bet your ass. That's right.

22
00:02:32,464 --> 00:02:35,843
Bought and paid for it. Except my supplier
ghosted once I put down.

23
00:02:35,926 --> 00:02:37,970
So, what'd you get for paying in advance?

24
00:02:38,053 --> 00:02:39,972
-I can't move.
-Shut it!

25
00:02:40,055 --> 00:02:44,435
She's got people. One of our own.
Just looking to make some fast scratch.

26
00:02:44,518 --> 00:02:46,228
She'd been curved for it too. Up to now.

27
00:02:46,312 --> 00:02:47,229
Hold on.

28
00:02:47,313 --> 00:02:49,732
-Huh?
-Your supplier. You mean…

29
00:02:49,815 --> 00:02:53,527
Gloria Martinez. That ring a bell?

30
00:02:53,611 --> 00:02:55,237
Oh, yeah. She's my mom.

31
00:02:55,321 --> 00:02:56,447
Huh?

32
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:58,407
So, you're Gloria's brat?

33
00:02:58,490 --> 00:03:00,367
Why did she think you can handle
an offer with you?

34
00:03:00,451 --> 00:03:01,869
She didn't. She died.

35
00:03:01,952 --> 00:03:03,412
Huh?

36
00:03:03,495 --> 00:03:04,455
Yesterday.

37
00:03:04,538 --> 00:03:08,250
What the fuck?
But I just talked to her two days ago.

38
00:03:08,334 --> 00:03:10,753
What happened?
The bad just killed get her, or--

39
00:03:10,836 --> 00:03:12,588
It was a car accident.

40
00:03:12,671 --> 00:03:16,258
From some kind of gang group drive-by…
Got caught in the crossfire.

41
00:03:16,342 --> 00:03:18,844
Nothing to do with the Sandevistan.

42
00:03:20,346 --> 00:03:21,555
Hmm.

43
00:03:22,348 --> 00:03:23,515
Hmm.

44
00:03:24,099 --> 00:03:26,727
Tracks why she never bought us back.

45
00:03:26,810 --> 00:03:29,521
Condolences, kid. That's tough, but still…

46
00:03:30,522 --> 00:03:33,776
Don't paid for a set
that makes things free and easy for you.

47
00:03:33,859 --> 00:03:36,028
Listen. I had no idea it was yours.

48
00:03:36,111 --> 00:03:37,738
Yeah, I've never been an escort

49
00:03:37,821 --> 00:03:40,282
chipping all the mails spectrum
my mom left lying around.

50
00:03:40,366 --> 00:03:41,951
Good times, good times.

51
00:03:42,034 --> 00:03:44,245
Christ! This twerp's
clearly got a screw lose!

52
00:03:44,328 --> 00:03:46,538
Back off. He didn't know
what he was doing.

53
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:50,542
You guys… are cyberpunks, aren't you?

54
00:03:55,756 --> 00:03:57,174
What's it to you?

55
00:03:58,300 --> 00:03:59,593
Let me keep the Sandy.

56
00:03:59,677 --> 00:04:02,137
Can't pay you back just now,
but I'll work it off.

57
00:04:02,221 --> 00:04:04,807
One gig at a time, long as it takes.

58
00:04:04,890 --> 00:04:07,893
Not good enough.
Shit's a military-grade.

59
00:04:07,977 --> 00:04:10,396
You can't just buy another off the shelf.

60
00:04:10,479 --> 00:04:12,731
Whatever you paid my mom,
I'll get it back.

61
00:04:12,815 --> 00:04:14,066
No deal.

62
00:04:14,149 --> 00:04:15,985
I said, no murder.

63
00:04:16,068 --> 00:04:18,445
Come on! Just give me a chance!

64
00:04:18,529 --> 00:04:21,490
Now that's funny.
I look like I run a preschool to you?

65
00:04:21,573 --> 00:04:23,450
I'll fire up the Sandevistan.

66
00:04:23,534 --> 00:04:27,538
Bullshit. Totally like you can't
boot it up without keeling over.

67
00:04:27,621 --> 00:04:29,456
This toddler's full of surprises.

68
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:30,833
-Hmm?
-Hmm? No.

69
00:04:30,916 --> 00:04:33,210
Body his size
would sizzle up after two hits.

70
00:04:33,294 --> 00:04:34,837
Tried eight. No sizzle.

71
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,130
-Hmm?
-Hmm?

72
00:04:36,213 --> 00:04:38,966
Come on. That's a lot of bunk
and we all know it.

73
00:04:39,049 --> 00:04:42,594
Yeah? Okay. Then how about I prove it?

74
00:04:43,178 --> 00:04:45,597
Whoa. Plant your ass back down.

75
00:04:45,681 --> 00:04:48,559
Yo! Chill out.
Just gonna clap this cig real quick.

76
00:04:48,642 --> 00:04:50,602
That's in up my sleeve… See?

77
00:04:50,686 --> 00:04:51,645
Wha--? Huh?

78
00:04:53,564 --> 00:04:55,941
-Aah!
-That makes nine today…

79
00:04:56,025 --> 00:04:57,985
No way. It's actually ten.

80
00:04:58,068 --> 00:05:01,071
Holy shit! What in the
fast forward fuck was that?

81
00:05:01,155 --> 00:05:02,281
Just give me a chance.

82
00:05:02,364 --> 00:05:04,992
A chance, huh? What kind?

83
00:05:05,617 --> 00:05:07,619
Easy. You take me out on a job.

84
00:05:08,454 --> 00:05:09,747
Won't fuck it up.

85
00:05:21,842 --> 00:05:23,969
Got quite a pay on you.
I'll give you that.

86
00:05:24,053 --> 00:05:25,929
Okay, kid. You get one chance.

87
00:05:26,013 --> 00:05:27,598
Oh, great. Here we go again.

88
00:05:27,681 --> 00:05:31,393
I owe it to Gloria, and maybe
the apple don't fall far. Hmm?

89
00:05:31,477 --> 00:05:32,603
You won't regret it.

90
00:05:32,686 --> 00:05:34,980
-Huh? He-- Hey!
-Chill.

91
00:05:35,064 --> 00:05:36,565
Just slotting a tracker.

92
00:05:36,648 --> 00:05:39,193
Wouldn't want you go on AWOL on us.

93
00:05:39,276 --> 00:05:40,569
I ain't gonna run.

94
00:05:40,652 --> 00:05:44,198
Yeah, yeah. I heard
that one before. A lot of times.

95
00:05:44,281 --> 00:05:46,283
Be hearing from me tomorrow.

96
00:05:51,830 --> 00:05:55,584
So, cyberpunks. Those were
the kind of peeps you roll with.

97
00:05:57,628 --> 00:05:58,629
Mm-hm.

98
00:05:59,838 --> 00:06:01,632
-Could've said some--
-Like what?

99
00:06:01,715 --> 00:06:04,218
Seems like a plan from the start.

100
00:06:04,301 --> 00:06:07,096
Maine wouldn't shut up about
this priced Sandy going missing

101
00:06:07,179 --> 00:06:10,015
and I saw you using
an exact same one in this train.

102
00:06:10,099 --> 00:06:13,060
Knew for sure you had his
after the visit to your reaper.

103
00:06:13,143 --> 00:06:16,105
Then thought you'd bat your eyes
at me till they showed.

104
00:06:16,939 --> 00:06:18,690
You're lying the whole time.

105
00:06:18,774 --> 00:06:20,526
Just go home already.

106
00:06:21,151 --> 00:06:22,194
Yeah.

107
00:06:27,699 --> 00:06:28,575
About your mom…

108
00:06:29,243 --> 00:06:30,828
Sorry for your loss.

109
00:07:00,315 --> 00:07:01,692
Mr. Martinez,

110
00:07:01,775 --> 00:07:06,488
wonderful news. Based on your
exemplary academic performance,

111
00:07:06,572 --> 00:07:09,491
the Arasaka Corporation
has awarded you a scholarship

112
00:07:09,575 --> 00:07:12,619
so that you may return to your studies.

113
00:07:12,703 --> 00:07:16,748
This is an exceptionally rare opportunity

114
00:07:16,832 --> 00:07:19,251
and a great honor. Congratulations.

115
00:07:19,334 --> 00:07:20,711
However,

116
00:07:20,794 --> 00:07:23,589
there is still the matter
of your recent violent behavior

117
00:07:23,672 --> 00:07:26,717
regarding Mr. Tanaka on Academy grounds.

118
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:28,886
Now, I spoke with Mr. Tanaka

119
00:07:28,969 --> 00:07:31,597
and he has graciously agreed

120
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:34,475
to strike several demerits
from your permanent record

121
00:07:34,558 --> 00:07:36,685
should you offer an apology.

122
00:07:36,768 --> 00:07:38,437
For details, please--

123
00:07:41,857 --> 00:07:42,900
Hmm?

124
00:07:42,983 --> 00:07:44,776
Kid, you're up.

125
00:07:54,995 --> 00:07:57,331
Hey! Over here, kid.

126
00:08:00,626 --> 00:08:02,336
Morning, sunshine. You ready?

127
00:08:02,419 --> 00:08:04,713
The data wasn't lying.
He is just a kid.

128
00:08:04,796 --> 00:08:06,924
-Can he keep up?
-Guess we'll see.

129
00:08:07,007 --> 00:08:09,843
Now I know.
I know he's a sweet little thing,

130
00:08:09,927 --> 00:08:11,970
but keep those grabbing myths to yourself.

131
00:08:12,054 --> 00:08:14,598
Why do we even put up with you?

132
00:08:15,265 --> 00:08:19,144
This one here is Kiwi.
And Dorio and Pilar, you've met.

133
00:08:19,228 --> 00:08:20,562
Make yourself comfy.

134
00:08:21,897 --> 00:08:23,690
-My name is David--
-Too fast.

135
00:08:23,774 --> 00:08:26,026
Let's get right down to biz, kid.

136
00:08:26,568 --> 00:08:27,903
Slot the shard.

137
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:36,328
Say hello to Arasaka Corporation's
driver and bodyguard…

138
00:08:36,411 --> 00:08:38,038
-Maxim.
-Yeah!

139
00:08:38,121 --> 00:08:41,667
We're gonna swipe the nav data
from the limo he rolls around the area.

140
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:44,211
Just the data? Not the car?

141
00:08:44,294 --> 00:08:45,379
We clap the ride

142
00:08:45,462 --> 00:08:48,298
and Arasaka's ninjas
will swarm us like flies to shit.

143
00:08:48,382 --> 00:08:50,509
So, yeah, just the data.

144
00:08:50,592 --> 00:08:51,718
How?

145
00:08:51,802 --> 00:08:55,222
Betting on fights
is this lad here's sole joy in life.

146
00:08:55,305 --> 00:08:57,766
He's in one of those seats every weekend.

147
00:08:59,059 --> 00:09:01,603
He always put a bag
stack on Butcher,

148
00:09:01,687 --> 00:09:04,189
bank them on its cold,
splitting, upper cutters.

149
00:09:06,316 --> 00:09:09,611
From hearing alone,
most peeps show up just to see her

150
00:09:09,695 --> 00:09:12,781
paint the cage red
with some poor gut's blood.

151
00:09:13,615 --> 00:09:14,616
Except…

152
00:09:20,038 --> 00:09:22,708
this weekend,
ain't gonna go down like that,

153
00:09:22,791 --> 00:09:27,337
the Butcher's getting butchered
in round one, like a sad sack of meat.

154
00:09:34,428 --> 00:09:35,721
What makes you so sure?

155
00:09:35,804 --> 00:09:38,223
Just trust me on that.

156
00:09:41,935 --> 00:09:43,145
Anyway,

157
00:09:43,228 --> 00:09:46,356
he had a habit of drowning the sorrows
at this one hole in a wall dive.

158
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:50,861
And that's where you make your move,
few drinks in when he's getting greased.

159
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,661
You nab the key and hand it to Dorio.

160
00:10:00,203 --> 00:10:02,497
She'll photocopy the pop block.

161
00:10:02,581 --> 00:10:07,169
Then we clap the nav data while
sack-of-muscle Max was still shit-faced.

162
00:10:08,337 --> 00:10:09,963
But leave that to us,

163
00:10:10,047 --> 00:10:13,175
you just got to slip the key back
in the slot before he catches on.

164
00:10:13,842 --> 00:10:15,844
That's it. Simple.

165
00:10:17,095 --> 00:10:17,971
Hold on…

166
00:10:18,055 --> 00:10:19,848
His master's calling.

167
00:10:19,931 --> 00:10:24,269
Sheesh, bastard can't catch
a break. No rest for the wicked.

168
00:10:24,353 --> 00:10:25,687
Not good.

169
00:10:25,771 --> 00:10:28,273
-His boss needs him there.
-Shit, on his day off?

170
00:10:28,357 --> 00:10:29,775
Data's not copied yet!

171
00:10:29,858 --> 00:10:32,486
Fuck! Change of plans, kid.

172
00:10:32,569 --> 00:10:34,404
Key to the car. Grab it.

173
00:10:35,072 --> 00:10:37,157
Becca, trip him up.

174
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,451
-Huh?
-Chop chop, go!

175
00:10:42,162 --> 00:10:44,206
-Aah!
-Hey! What the fuck?

176
00:10:44,289 --> 00:10:47,918
-I'm so clumsy. Sorry!
-Watch it, kid! Ooh!

177
00:10:49,252 --> 00:10:52,047
Get in. Nab the data
before he shows.

178
00:10:52,881 --> 00:10:53,882
How in the hell?

179
00:10:53,965 --> 00:10:55,801
I'll handle that.

180
00:10:56,426 --> 00:10:57,302
You get in.

181
00:11:00,097 --> 00:11:02,307
Ahh…

182
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:07,771
Man…

183
00:11:08,522 --> 00:11:09,439
You good?

184
00:11:09,523 --> 00:11:10,691
Don't talk. Focusing.

185
00:11:11,441 --> 00:11:14,695
Arasaka eyes was such
a huge pain in the ass.

186
00:11:15,529 --> 00:11:17,155
Sorry about that, handsome!

187
00:11:17,239 --> 00:11:20,075
Nah. It's no problem, sweetheart.

188
00:11:20,158 --> 00:11:22,119
I'll make it up to you next time. Okay?

189
00:11:22,202 --> 00:11:24,496
Oh?

190
00:11:24,579 --> 00:11:26,623
-You, bitch!
-Why are you yelling at me?

191
00:11:26,707 --> 00:11:28,959
You're so sensitive, you know!

192
00:11:29,042 --> 00:11:30,919
We're blown. Target coming in hot.

193
00:11:31,002 --> 00:11:32,838
-Stats?
-Just a little more.

194
00:11:32,921 --> 00:11:34,256
Time's up. Cut it!

195
00:11:34,339 --> 00:11:36,091
Almost…

196
00:11:36,174 --> 00:11:37,592
Ahh. Done.

197
00:11:37,676 --> 00:11:39,219
It won't open!

198
00:11:39,302 --> 00:11:41,138
The security's back online?

199
00:11:41,221 --> 00:11:43,223
Like I said, time's up.

200
00:11:43,306 --> 00:11:46,184
Open up! Now! You, fuck!

201
00:11:46,852 --> 00:11:49,312
Oh, shit. No way back.

202
00:11:49,396 --> 00:11:50,522
-Start her up.
-What?

203
00:11:50,605 --> 00:11:51,773
Punch it, kid.

204
00:11:51,857 --> 00:11:53,775
I don't know how to drive!

205
00:11:53,859 --> 00:11:55,902
Time to work.

206
00:11:55,986 --> 00:11:58,405
Hey! Hey!

207
00:11:58,488 --> 00:12:00,741
Get out! I said!

208
00:12:00,824 --> 00:12:02,784
-Show me…
-You're dead meat!

209
00:12:02,868 --> 00:12:04,327
…you got what it takes.

210
00:12:04,411 --> 00:12:05,996
You hear me?

211
00:12:06,079 --> 00:12:10,417
I'll make you and your whole family pay!

212
00:12:11,585 --> 00:12:13,712
Hey! Stop! My car!

213
00:12:20,177 --> 00:12:23,597
Wait! I said, wait!

214
00:12:26,057 --> 00:12:28,268
Sure glad them ain't my wheels.

215
00:12:28,351 --> 00:12:31,813
Take it straight to Aldo's.
You hash the GPS?

216
00:12:31,897 --> 00:12:34,316
Can't from inside. Got a jammer up,

217
00:12:34,399 --> 00:12:37,652
but encryption's shaky.
They'll snatch our position soon,

218
00:12:37,736 --> 00:12:39,571
unless we find solid cover.

219
00:12:39,654 --> 00:12:43,366
Then Aldo's it is.
Should be safe there. On our way.

220
00:12:43,450 --> 00:12:45,410
Ah, fuck, communications cutting out.

221
00:12:45,494 --> 00:12:46,536
-Do I pull over?
-No!

222
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:50,207
Geo stats ping you,
they'll drop a hit squad on your ass.

223
00:12:50,290 --> 00:12:51,500
Drive like hell!

224
00:12:52,876 --> 00:12:54,878
-Summing a route.
-Thank you.

225
00:12:56,129 --> 00:12:59,466
-You think we can make it?
-It's up to you now.

226
00:13:01,885 --> 00:13:04,596
Look at you. You're practically a pro.

227
00:13:04,679 --> 00:13:05,722
You think so?

228
00:13:05,806 --> 00:13:08,141
I mean, maybe if autopilot wasn't on.

229
00:13:08,225 --> 00:13:09,851
Whatever.

230
00:13:09,935 --> 00:13:11,061
We've got company.

231
00:13:11,603 --> 00:13:12,646
Huh?

232
00:13:12,729 --> 00:13:14,856
Tyger Claws?

233
00:13:16,233 --> 00:13:19,528
Maxim must've
provide them with a new ride.

234
00:13:19,611 --> 00:13:22,113
-That fast?
-Best if we don't fuck with corpos.

235
00:13:22,197 --> 00:13:24,407
Make up the advantage down here on bikes.

236
00:13:24,491 --> 00:13:25,909
Get the highway here.

237
00:13:27,744 --> 00:13:29,704
Why are you running?

238
00:13:29,788 --> 00:13:30,872
Come backand fight, cowards!

239
00:13:30,956 --> 00:13:34,668
Where are you going?

240
00:13:34,751 --> 00:13:36,586
Gotta lose these guys.

241
00:13:37,170 --> 00:13:38,672
Shit. Traffic?

242
00:13:38,755 --> 00:13:40,131
Oh, my, my…

243
00:13:40,757 --> 00:13:42,425
Not good.

244
00:13:57,274 --> 00:13:59,192
Uh… Closing in on us.

245
00:13:59,276 --> 00:14:00,694
Slow-ass!

246
00:14:02,779 --> 00:14:05,198
-Put your buckle up!
-Huh?

247
00:14:17,335 --> 00:14:19,546
How dare you do that to my partner!

248
00:14:33,226 --> 00:14:35,604
Don't underestimate me!

249
00:15:04,716 --> 00:15:06,092
Seems shut-tied.

250
00:15:06,176 --> 00:15:07,802
Aldo should be inside.

251
00:15:07,886 --> 00:15:10,639
Well, at least the jammer
is still running stable.

252
00:15:12,474 --> 00:15:13,642
The doors weren't locked?

253
00:15:13,725 --> 00:15:16,269
Then unlocked for a while.

254
00:15:16,353 --> 00:15:18,355
Stay here. I'll scoop it out.

255
00:15:30,367 --> 00:15:32,827
Come on now, don't run away.

256
00:15:32,911 --> 00:15:35,413
Let's play a little more!

257
00:15:57,727 --> 00:15:58,770
Die!

258
00:16:01,648 --> 00:16:04,275
Die!

259
00:16:39,102 --> 00:16:40,145
Ew…

260
00:16:41,021 --> 00:16:44,399
Ugh!

261
00:16:46,443 --> 00:16:47,652
Sorry for the wait.

262
00:16:56,244 --> 00:16:58,163
Yee-ha!

263
00:16:58,246 --> 00:17:01,916
Yeah!

264
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:05,628
Well, gotta say not bad for wookie-wookie.

265
00:17:05,712 --> 00:17:07,130
So, we're cool now?

266
00:17:07,213 --> 00:17:09,340
Sure. Welcome to the crew.

267
00:17:11,217 --> 00:17:12,552
But remember, little man.

268
00:17:13,219 --> 00:17:16,556
Ain't no one in this world
you can trust more than yourself.

269
00:17:20,143 --> 00:17:22,604
Start using us as your crutch,
and you're good as dead.

270
00:17:22,687 --> 00:17:23,897
Mm-hm.

271
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:25,148
Yeah, got you.

272
00:17:27,901 --> 00:17:33,198
Yee-ha!

273
00:17:33,281 --> 00:17:36,201
Check out the precision, dudes!
Fastest thing, isn't it?

274
00:17:36,284 --> 00:17:38,828
I know the only thing that hurts
fastest in the west.

275
00:17:41,831 --> 00:17:43,833
Spit it! Devoted, you say?

276
00:17:45,418 --> 00:17:48,630
All hands on me!
You wanna take up for a test drive?

277
00:17:50,882 --> 00:17:51,925
Thanks.

278
00:17:54,302 --> 00:17:57,305
Immunoblockers.
Enough to get you through a month.

279
00:17:57,847 --> 00:17:59,474
And…

280
00:17:59,557 --> 00:18:01,267
Here's your cut.

281
00:18:01,351 --> 00:18:02,602
Holy shit!

282
00:18:02,685 --> 00:18:06,106
Everybody gets a fair shake.
Only where I operate.

283
00:18:07,899 --> 00:18:09,984
-You still mostly organic?
-Huh?

284
00:18:10,068 --> 00:18:13,321
Save some heads,
then look in to open your cyberware.

285
00:18:13,404 --> 00:18:16,866
Mere bone can't keep page
with the Sandevistan for long.

286
00:18:16,950 --> 00:18:18,201
You've got a point.

287
00:18:18,284 --> 00:18:22,664
Little more chrome and you could've zeroed
that Tyger Claw no prop,

288
00:18:22,747 --> 00:18:24,624
or any goon out there.

289
00:18:27,836 --> 00:18:32,382
It ain't waste of 'ennies if it makes you
stronger. That applies to your cyberware.

290
00:18:32,465 --> 00:18:33,633
And also,

291
00:18:33,716 --> 00:18:34,968
to your crew.

292
00:18:35,051 --> 00:18:37,303
Yeah, alright.

293
00:18:37,387 --> 00:18:41,641
Oh.

294
00:18:49,858 --> 00:18:50,942
Shit…

295
00:18:57,866 --> 00:19:01,911
I believe I was clear when I requested
only the navigation data,

296
00:19:01,995 --> 00:19:04,455
not Arasaka's corporate property.

297
00:19:04,539 --> 00:19:06,624
You got what you
asked for, didn't you?

298
00:19:06,708 --> 00:19:10,211
What I asked for above all else
was your discretion in the matter.

299
00:19:10,295 --> 00:19:12,964
We tried, but you know
how things be sometimes.

300
00:19:13,047 --> 00:19:14,465
Gotta improvise.

301
00:19:14,549 --> 00:19:18,261
It was imperative I learned
Tanaka's routines the places he frequents.

302
00:19:18,344 --> 00:19:21,556
So check the navigation data.
It's all there.

303
00:19:21,639 --> 00:19:25,768
Your joyride put us back at square one
and Tanaka on high alert.

304
00:19:25,852 --> 00:19:28,104
He's already switch sides.
The data is useless.

305
00:19:28,188 --> 00:19:29,981
Okay, switched and sided for what?

306
00:19:30,064 --> 00:19:31,441
That's not for you to know.

307
00:19:31,524 --> 00:19:35,695
Damn! How the hell we supposed to do the
job right when you leave us in the dark?

308
00:19:35,778 --> 00:19:40,408
The less you know, the less I risk.
Understand this and understand it fast.

309
00:19:40,491 --> 00:19:42,076
I do not pay you to think.

310
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:44,954
I pay you to check the boxes off my list.

311
00:19:45,038 --> 00:19:47,665
It is my place
to see the larger picture.

312
00:19:47,749 --> 00:19:50,752
It is yours to listen.
You will do what you're told.

313
00:19:50,835 --> 00:19:52,962
That is how our business is done.

314
00:19:53,755 --> 00:19:55,298
Are we clear?

315
00:19:58,426 --> 00:20:01,012
Yeah, we're crystal, dude.

316
00:20:01,095 --> 00:20:05,391
Very good. For now, we'll wait
until he lowers his guard again.

317
00:20:05,475 --> 00:20:06,809
I'll be in touch.

318
00:20:06,893 --> 00:20:09,229
Uh-huh. See you.

319
00:20:13,233 --> 00:20:14,400
Who was that?

320
00:20:15,193 --> 00:20:18,696
Faraday. The middleman
who landed us the gig.

321
00:20:18,780 --> 00:20:21,741
He happens to be a top fixer
around these ports.

322
00:20:22,742 --> 00:20:25,203
Thought you were the big boss
making all the calls.

323
00:20:25,286 --> 00:20:29,832
No, I'm the guy who gets shit done.
And he's the one holding all the 'ennies.

324
00:20:29,916 --> 00:20:33,711
Without him and his crutch,
you ain't nothing in this biz.

325
00:20:33,795 --> 00:20:35,380
It's as simple as that.

326
00:20:36,714 --> 00:20:38,883
Don't think too hard about it.

327
00:20:38,967 --> 00:20:40,927
We're celebrating tonight.

328
00:20:41,678 --> 00:20:42,679
Mm.

329
00:20:54,107 --> 00:20:57,402
Heh-heh-heh!

330
00:20:59,487 --> 00:21:03,491
Hey, baby! What do you say, huh?

331
00:21:05,910 --> 00:21:07,912
-Yo.
-Mm.

332
00:21:08,496 --> 00:21:10,248
Um, sorry, but, who are you?

333
00:21:10,331 --> 00:21:13,835
Remember. Come on,
after all we've bee through?

334
00:21:13,918 --> 00:21:15,253
Hmm.

335
00:21:18,381 --> 00:21:20,300
Oh, right. You were at the bar.

336
00:21:20,383 --> 00:21:22,343
Yeah. You like my performance?

337
00:21:22,427 --> 00:21:24,178
-Uh, sure. Yeah.
-Mm.

338
00:21:24,929 --> 00:21:28,558
I'm Rebecca.
I heard you're joining up on Maine's crew?

339
00:21:28,641 --> 00:21:31,311
Maybe. Is this carbonated?

340
00:21:31,394 --> 00:21:32,812
Cheers!

341
00:21:32,895 --> 00:21:36,065
Be seeing you around, then. Bu-bye!

342
00:21:36,149 --> 00:21:37,567
Yeah. See you.

343
00:21:45,450 --> 00:21:50,163
Mr. Martinez, hello again.
Is this a good time?

344
00:21:50,246 --> 00:21:51,831
It sounds rather rowdy on your end.

345
00:21:52,749 --> 00:21:54,334
Uh, yeah, but it's fine.

346
00:21:54,417 --> 00:21:57,545
I trust you received
the message that I left?

347
00:21:57,628 --> 00:21:59,255
Yeah, I got it.

348
00:21:59,339 --> 00:22:01,799
Excellent. Now, about your apology to--

349
00:22:01,883 --> 00:22:04,218
Pass this along
to Katsuo for me, would you?

350
00:22:04,302 --> 00:22:06,095
Er, perhaps it's best if you would--

351
00:22:06,179 --> 00:22:09,349
If he wants revenge,
tell that prick I'll be waiting.

352
00:22:09,432 --> 00:22:10,850
But I'm done going easy.

353
00:22:10,933 --> 00:22:12,518
Oh, and you can all kiss my ass!
